<title>TURKEY: Turk Migros 96 profits rise 88 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Migros 96 profits rise 88 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   2,491.38  vs  1,989.17</p>
<p>    Net profit		    1,345.35  vs    716.10</p>
<p>    Net sales		    45,375.29  vs 19,313.11</p>
<p>    Operating loss		  384.86  vs    314.29 profit</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  2,044.49  vs    757.95</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		     0     vs	 0</p>
<p>    Total debts		  10,993.21  vs  4,880.58</p>
<p>    Equity			  3,203.98  vs  1,564.97</p>
<p>    Capital			   540.00  vs    360.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's leading supermarket chain Migros Turk A.S. is owned 55.11 percent by Temel Ticaret, an affiliate of the leading industrial conglomerate Koc Holding.</p>
<p>The company plans to pay a 500 lira cash dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share from its 1996 profits after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders on March 31.</p>
<p>It also plans to raise its capital to 945 billion lira by issuing 405 billion lira of bonuses, or 0.75 bonus for one existing share.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
